---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { PUBLIC_SITE_URL } from 'astro:env/client';

const seoTitle = 'Comegame vs Other Online Gaming Platforms: Full Comparison Guide';
const seoDescription =
	'Detailed comparison of Comegame against Dream11, MPL, and other platforms — features, usability, rewards, and who should choose what.';
const canonicalUrl = `${PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/blog/comegame-vs-other-online-gaming-platforms`;
const ogImage = `${PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/android-chrome-512x512.png`;
const keywordsMeta =
	'comegame vs dream11, comegame vs mpl, online gaming platforms india, best gaming app india, comegame comparison, dream11 alternative';

const articleSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'BlogPosting',
	headline: seoTitle,
	description: seoDescription,
	url: canonicalUrl,
	image: ogImage,
	datePublished: '2026-03-24',
	dateModified: '2026-07-02',
	inLanguage: 'en-IN',
	author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Come Game Guide' },
	publisher: {
		'@type': 'Organization',
		name: 'Come Game Guide',
		logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: ogImage },
	},
	mainEntityOfPage: canonicalUrl,
};

const faqSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'FAQPage',
	mainEntity: [
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Is Comegame better than Dream11?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Comegame and Dream11 serve different audiences. Dream11 focuses on fantasy sports while Comegame offers direct skill-game mechanics with a simpler interface. The better choice depends on whether you prefer fantasy team-building or direct skill-based play.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Does Comegame have lower entry fees than MPL?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Entry fees vary by contest type on both platforms. Comegame typically offers a range of entry points including free practice modes. Always check current contest listings for the most up-to-date fee structures.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Which platform is best for beginners in India?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Comegame is frequently recommended for beginners because of its simpler interface, low device requirements, and accessible onboarding process. Vision11 is another beginner-friendly option.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Can I use Comegame on a budget Android phone?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Yes. Comegame is designed to work on mid-range Android devices with standard mobile internet connections, making it more accessible than graphics-heavy gaming platforms.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Is real money gaming legal on all these platforms in India?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: "Real money gaming laws vary by state in India. Always check your local regulations before participating in paid contests on any platform. Skill-based games are generally permitted under central law but some states have specific restrictions.",
			},
		},
	],
};
---

<Layout
	title={seoTitle}
	description={seoDescription}
	keywords={keywordsMeta}
	canonical={canonicalUrl}
	ogImage={ogImage}
>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)}></script>
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)}></script>
	</Fragment>

	<article class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-16">
		<header class="max-w-4xl">
			<a
				href="/blog"
				class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-border bg-card px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground"
			>
				Back to Blog
			</a>
			<h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-5xl">
				Comegame vs Other Online Gaming Platforms: Full Comparison Guide
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-muted-foreground">Published on March 24, 2026 | Updated July 2, 2026 | Comparison Guide</p>
			<p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground md:text-lg">
				India's online gaming market has grown dramatically over the past few years, and with that growth
				comes a crowded field of platforms competing for your attention. Choosing between Comegame, Dream11,
				MPL, My11Circle, and PlayerzPot is not straightforward — each platform has genuine strengths
				and distinct trade-offs. This guide gives you a structured, honest comparison so you can make
				an informed decision based on your skill level, preferred game type, and device.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="mt-10 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Why This Comparison Matters for Indian Users</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				India now has over 500 million smartphone users and one of the world's fastest-growing mobile
				internet bases. Online gaming has moved from a niche activity to mainstream entertainment, with
				real-money skill games forming a significant and legally recognised segment. But the sheer number
				of available platforms creates a genuine problem: information overload. Users searching for the
				best platform often encounter promotional content designed to push them toward one option without
				fairly representing others.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The stakes are real. If you deposit money on a platform that does not match your skill level or
				preferred game type, you are more likely to lose quickly and form a negative opinion of gaming
				altogether. Understanding what each platform actually offers — and who each one is genuinely built
				for — is the first step toward a sustainable, enjoyable experience. Before diving into comparisons,
				it helps to read the <a href="/come-games" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Come Games overview</a>
				to understand what game categories Comegame specifically offers.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				This guide focuses on five platforms that appear most frequently in Indian user searches: Comegame,
				Dream11, MPL, My11Circle, and PlayerzPot. We compare them across interface design, game variety,
				device performance, entry fees, bonus structures, payment systems, and responsible gaming features.
				No single platform wins every category — the goal is to map each one to the right type of user.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">What Makes Comegame Different</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame occupies a distinct position in the Indian gaming market. While most established platforms
				were built around fantasy sports or specific game genres, Comegame was designed from the ground up
				around simplicity and accessibility. The interface is deliberately clean — no cluttered promotional
				banners, no overwhelming menu structures, no feature overload on the home screen. Users who open
				the app for the first time can identify core functions within minutes rather than needing a tutorial.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The mobile performance story is equally strong. Comegame is optimised for mid-range Android devices
				running on 4G connections — the precise setup that describes the majority of Indian gamers outside
				metro areas. This is not an accident. Heavy platforms that demand high-end processors and Wi-Fi
				connections effectively exclude a significant portion of the Indian gaming audience. Comegame's
				technical architecture makes it genuinely usable on a ₹8,000–₹15,000 smartphone.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The onboarding process is another differentiator. Registration on Comegame takes under five minutes.
				There are no complex team-selection tutorials, no sport-specific knowledge requirements, and no steep
				learning curve before your first game. This low barrier makes it a natural starting point for users
				who are new to online gaming altogether. If you haven't installed the platform yet, the
				<a href="/download-come-games-app" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Come Game app download guide</a>
				walks you through the safest installation method and what to check before running the file.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame also distinguishes itself through game mechanics. Rather than building teams from real
				athletes and scoring points based on match statistics — the core fantasy sports model — Comegame
				centres on direct skill-based games where the player's own actions determine the outcome. This is
				a fundamentally different mental model that appeals to users who want their performance to be the
				primary variable, not athlete selection or sports knowledge.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Comegame vs Dream11: Different Games for Different Mindsets</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Dream11 is India's most recognised online gaming platform and, for many users, the default first
				choice. It pioneered the fantasy sports format in India, building a massive community of cricket,
				football, kabaddi, and basketball fans who build virtual teams from real players and earn points
				based on live match performance. Dream11's strength is its deep integration with Indian sports
				culture — if you follow cricket closely and enjoy analysing player form and pitch conditions,
				Dream11 gives that knowledge genuine value.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The complexity, however, is real. To consistently do well on Dream11, users need sport-specific
				knowledge, an understanding of statistical patterns, and the ability to read match conditions before
				selection. There are research tools within the app — recent form data, head-to-head records, expert
				picks — but using them effectively requires time and sports literacy. Beginners without this
				background often find the platform opaque. The contest structures add another layer: Grand Leagues
				with thousands of participants offer large prizes but very low win probabilities, while smaller
				head-to-head formats give better odds but smaller rewards. Navigating this intelligently is a skill
				in itself.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame, by contrast, requires no external sports knowledge. You compete based on your in-game
				performance directly, without needing to predict how a real-world athlete will perform on any given
				day. This makes Comegame more consistent — your skill level is the primary variable, not external
				match events you cannot control. For users who want skill to directly determine outcomes, this is
				a significant advantage. Read the detailed breakdown of what Comegame games involve on the
				<a href="/come-games" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Come Games page</a>
				to see how each format works in practice.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Audience profile matters here. Dream11 is best for users who are active sports followers and enjoy
				the research and team-selection process as part of the game. Comegame is better for users who want
				direct, performance-based outcomes without requiring sport-specific expertise. These are genuinely
				different value propositions — one is not objectively better, but the fit depends entirely on
				what you enjoy. Our
				<a href="/blog/best-dream11-alternatives-india-comegame" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">best Dream11 alternatives guide</a>
				covers this trade-off in more detail alongside other options worth considering.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Comegame vs MPL: Game Variety and User Experience</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Mobile Premier League (MPL) takes a broad-platform approach. It hosts an enormous variety of
				game types — casual arcade games, fantasy sports, puzzle games, board games, and esports
				tournaments — all within a single app. This breadth is MPL's defining feature and its biggest
				selling point for users who enjoy switching between game types based on mood or available time.
				If you spend fifteen minutes in the morning on a casual puzzle and two hours in the evening on
				a fantasy cricket contest, MPL accommodates both without requiring separate apps.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The trade-off for that variety is complexity. MPL's interface handles a significant number of
				game categories, promotional events, and tournament structures simultaneously. For experienced
				users who enjoy exploring a platform and discovering new formats, this is a positive. For users
				who want a streamlined, focused experience — get in, play the one type of game they enjoy, track
				performance, get out — MPL can feel overwhelming. Notifications are frequent, promotional offers
				are numerous, and the home screen can feel cluttered compared to simpler alternatives.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Entry fees on MPL range widely — from free practice games to paid contests with substantial
				prize pools. The casual game side of MPL often has very low minimum entry points (₹1–₹5 per
				game), which reduces the financial barrier for experimentation. Fantasy sports contests on MPL
				follow similar pricing structures to Dream11.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame versus MPL ultimately comes down to focus versus breadth. If you want one platform
				with the widest possible game catalogue and you enjoy the discovery aspect of a large app,
				MPL serves that need well. If you want a faster, cleaner experience centred on skill-based
				direct play without navigating through a broad entertainment catalogue, Comegame is the more
				efficient choice. Understanding how these platforms technically deliver their games can also
				help you choose — the
				<a href="/blog/how-online-gaming-platforms-like-comegame-operate" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">guide on how online gaming platforms operate</a>
				explains the infrastructure differences that affect the user experience.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Comegame vs My11Circle and PlayerzPot</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				My11Circle is the closest structural competitor to Dream11 — a fantasy sports platform with
				strong cricket coverage and a user base that largely migrated from Dream11 or uses both
				simultaneously. My11Circle differentiates itself with a cleaner interface than Dream11,
				slightly less congested contest structures during peak cricket events, and occasional promotional
				incentives for new users. For someone who loves fantasy cricket and is looking for a Dream11
				alternative rather than a different type of gaming experience, My11Circle is a natural second
				choice.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				PlayerzPot takes a wider multi-sport view. It covers cricket, football, basketball, kabaddi,
				and volleyball within its fantasy framework, which appeals to users who want to switch sports
				across seasons without moving platforms. PlayerzPot's interface is stable and well-maintained,
				and it has earned a reasonable reputation for reliability — contests fill up as listed, withdrawals
				process within stated timelines, and customer support is responsive. For serious fantasy players
				who want multi-sport coverage and a dependable experience, PlayerzPot is worth considering.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Where Comegame separates itself from both My11Circle and PlayerzPot is the fundamental game
				model. Both those platforms are fantasy sports — your performance depends on athlete selection
				and real-world match outcomes. Comegame is direct skill gaming — your performance depends on
				your own in-game execution. This is the decisive factor. If fantasy sports is what you want,
				My11Circle and PlayerzPot are both well-built options. If you want outcomes that your own
				skill determines directly, Comegame is the right category. Visit the
				<a href="/" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame homepage</a>
				for an overview of how the platform positions itself within this context.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Feature Comparison: Narrative Overview</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Rather than a raw table, here is a narrative comparison of how each platform performs across
				the most important features for Indian users.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Interface simplicity:</strong> Comegame ranks highest here. Its
				stripped-back design reduces friction at every step. Dream11 and MPL both have feature-rich
				interfaces that reward experienced users but can overwhelm newcomers. My11Circle and PlayerzPot
				sit in the middle — functional and well-organised, but more complex than Comegame.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Game variety:</strong> MPL leads significantly, with dozens of
				game categories. Dream11 offers the widest fantasy sports coverage. PlayerzPot covers multiple
				sports within fantasy. My11Circle focuses on cricket. Comegame offers focused skill-game
				categories rather than a broad catalogue — a deliberate choice that prioritises depth over width.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Skill dependency:</strong> Comegame is the most skill-dependent
				in the direct play sense. Fantasy sports on Dream11, My11Circle, and PlayerzPot are legally
				classified as skill games, but the skill involves knowledge of sports and statistics rather than
				direct in-game execution. MPL varies widely — casual arcade games are largely luck-based; fantasy
				contests on MPL are skill-classified.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Beginner accessibility:</strong> Comegame is the most accessible
				for complete beginners — no prerequisite sports knowledge, no complex team-building mechanics,
				and a fast onboarding path. Dream11 and My11Circle assume sports familiarity. MPL is accessible
				on its casual game side but complex overall. PlayerzPot requires multi-sport understanding.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Community and competition scale:</strong> Dream11 has the largest
				active user base in India by a significant margin, which means contest pools fill faster and
				prize pools can be substantial. MPL has a large casual gaming community. Comegame, My11Circle,
				and PlayerzPot have smaller but more focused communities. This affects contest availability
				during non-peak hours — smaller platforms may have fewer contest options late at night or
				during off-season periods.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Performance and Device Requirements</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Device compatibility is a practical barrier that many comparison articles overlook. In India,
				a large proportion of mobile gamers use devices in the ₹6,000–₹15,000 price range — phones with
				2GB–4GB RAM, mid-tier processors, and reliance on 4G rather than home broadband. How well a
				platform runs on this class of device is a genuine differentiator.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame is specifically optimised for this segment. The app has a modest storage footprint,
				loads quickly on standard 4G, and does not rely on high-end GPU processing for its game
				mechanics. Users consistently report smooth performance on budget Android devices — which
				is one of the primary reasons the platform has grown quickly in Tier-2 and Tier-3 cities.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Dream11 runs adequately on most mid-range phones but becomes slower during high-traffic
				periods — IPL season contest windows, for example, often see significant server loads that
				cause app lag at the moment of team submission. This is a known pain point for Dream11 users.
				MPL's performance varies depending on which specific game you are playing — fantasy contests
				are comparable to Dream11, while some of the arcade and casual games require more processing
				power and can lag on very low-end devices.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				My11Circle and PlayerzPot both perform reasonably well on mid-range devices. Neither requires
				high-end hardware, and both have made efforts to keep their app sizes manageable. However,
				neither matches Comegame's level of optimisation for truly budget devices.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Internet dependency also matters. All real-time gaming platforms require a stable connection.
				Comegame's game mechanics are designed with lower bandwidth requirements, which gives it an
				edge in areas with variable mobile signal quality. For users in regions where 4G signal is
				inconsistent, this is a practical advantage. The
				<a href="/blog/how-online-gaming-platforms-like-comegame-operate" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">technical guide on how gaming platforms operate</a>
				explains the role of server latency and connection quality in more depth.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Bonus and Promotion Structures Across Platforms</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Every major platform uses bonuses as a user acquisition and retention tool. Understanding
				the mechanics behind these offers is essential before you claim anything.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Dream11's promotional structure includes referral bonuses, welcome cash, and seasonal
				promotions tied to cricket tournaments. The welcome offers are typically significant in
				headline value but come with wagering or usage conditions — bonus cash often has to be
				used within contests before it can contribute to withdrawable winnings. During IPL, Dream11
				runs large-scale promotions with substantial prize pools that attract millions of entries,
				which simultaneously increases prize pool size and decreases win probability.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				MPL's bonus structure is complex because it covers multiple game types. Casual game bonuses
				often differ from fantasy sports bonuses on the same platform. New user offers vary by
				market and device. MPL also uses a token or coin system for some game types, which adds
				a conversion layer between in-app currency and real withdrawable money — always understand
				these conversion rates before participating.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame's promotion structure is more straightforward. Welcome bonuses, referral rewards,
				and periodic event promotions are offered, but the terms tend to be clearer and less
				layered than those on larger platforms. This transparency is part of the brand's positioning
				toward beginner users who may not have experience reading complex bonus terms. Always read
				the full terms on any platform before claiming. Our
				<a href="/real-money-come-games" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">real money Come Games guide</a>
				explains how to evaluate bonus offers fairly and what conditions to look for before accepting.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Payment and Withdrawal Comparison</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Payment infrastructure is where platform differences become most practically significant. A
				platform that processes withdrawals slowly or has unclear TDS (Tax Deducted at Source) policies
				creates real financial friction regardless of how enjoyable the gameplay is.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Dream11 supports UPI, net banking, debit cards, and popular digital wallets. Withdrawals are
				generally processed within 24–48 hours, with KYC verification required for amounts above
				a threshold. TDS at 30% is applied on net winnings above ₹10,000 per financial year under
				current Indian tax rules (as of 2025–26). Dream11's scale means its payment infrastructure
				is well-established and reliable, though peak period withdrawals can take slightly longer.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				MPL supports similar payment methods with UPI being the primary option for most Indian users.
				Withdrawal timelines are comparable to Dream11. One point of note on MPL is the multi-currency
				nature of the platform — some game winnings are in "MPL tokens" that convert to cash at specific
				rates, while others are directly in rupees. Understanding which currency applies to your specific
				game type before playing prevents confusion at withdrawal time.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame, My11Circle, and PlayerzPot all use UPI as the primary transaction method, which
				is the practical standard in India for fast, low-friction payments. Minimum withdrawal
				thresholds and processing times should be verified directly on the platform since these
				terms update periodically. For all platforms, completing KYC verification early in your
				journey — before you have winnings to withdraw — is the single best way to avoid delays.
				Our <a href="/faq" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">FAQ section</a>
				addresses common payment questions that apply across multiple platforms.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Who Should Choose Comegame vs Alternatives</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				After comparing all five platforms, the recommendation framework becomes clear. The right
				platform is determined by three factors: your game preference, your skill/knowledge base,
				and your device situation.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Choose Comegame if:</strong> you are new to online gaming
				and want a fast, non-intimidating entry point; you prefer direct skill-based games where
				your own performance determines outcomes; you play on a mid-range or budget Android device;
				you want a clean, focused interface without the complexity of fantasy team selection; or
				you are looking for a platform optimised for lower-bandwidth environments. The
				<a href="/blog/how-comegame-works-features-gameplay-basics" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">complete guide to how Comegame works</a>
				is the best next resource if this matches your profile.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
